cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Starpi in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Starpi"
abstract: "Knowledge assistant in the browser that shows how far each answer can be trusted: retrieval-augmented generation with verifiable citations, a deterministic source check that compares every statement with the excerpts it cites (facts, reversed negations, names and values in the wrong place, and relations between values and events), a sentence gate that releases a streamed sentence only once its numbers are backed, answer receipts with a Merkle tree and a device signature that anyone can verify against the original files, and commands that check documents in CI and write SARIF. Files are read and indexed on the device in a persistent workspace with hybrid retrieval; answers come from on-device models (WebGPU or WebAssembly), your own server, a local companion on your machine, or cloud providers with your own key or the site's key pools through a stateless relay, in a verified source mode or a free chat mode with voice, research jobs and tools. Six interface languages."
authors:
